    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-079 — Line-by-line float wrap (Proposed, diagnosis only).**\n\nDiagnostic data from ADR-074 traces confirmed that Wikipedia's `<h2>History` at `y≈2210` (Firefox: `y≈500`) is entirely due to ADR-031's block-narrowing approximation. Same root cause fixes both ADR-074 bugs (A: infobox positioning, B: block-narrowing over-stretch).\n\n## The measured problem\n\nAt 984px content width:\n- Infobox float: `y=799.1, h=738.4, bottom=1545.5`\n- 3 intro paragraphs precede History\n- Each paragraph is narrowed for its **full height** (instead of just lines overlapping the float)\n- Each paragraph is ~150-200px taller than Firefox's line-wrapped version\n- Total offset: ~1700px\n\nFirefox wraps line-by-line: only lines vertically overlapping the float narrow. Lines below the float use full width.\n\n## The proposed fix\n\n**Scope:** ~300-400 lines, 1-2 sessions. Medium risk — touches the most complex part of the layout engine.\n\n**Data model:**\n- New `FloatContext{left_w, right_w, bottom}` struct\n- Carried through inline layout chain\n\n**Algorithm:**\n- `break_styled_words_into_lines` becomes float-aware: evaluates available width per line based on current y range\n- `flatten_inline_to_words` passes `float_ctx` through\n- `layout_block_children` removes block-narrowing, relies on line-wrap inside\n\n**What stays the same:**\n- Float placement (ADR-031)\n- `clear` handling\n- Block-level float avoidance (blocks still jump past floats, per CSS spec)\n\n## Expected outcome\n\n| Metric | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `<h2>History` y (default) | 2210 | **~500** |\n| Infobox y (default) | 799 | **~267** |\n| Overall page height | 31000 | **~29400** |\n\nBoth ADR-074 bugs resolved from one root-cause fix.\n\n## This is the 6-session debt\n\nADR-032 was written to defer line-wrap implementation. The comment in `layout.cpp:1224` says:\n\n> *\"Full per-line text-wrap is deferred to ADR-032; this is a block-narrowing approximation that covers the infobox case.\"*\n\nADR-079 is that finally-landed completion.\n\n## What this does NOT do\n\n- Mobile menu at desktop width (ADR-076-D `:where()`/`:has()`)\n- `@media (min-width:...)` custom properties (ADR-078 deferred)\n- Font-metrics mismatch (ADR-070 deferred `measure_with_pango`)\n\n## Test count\n\n707 / 2670 unchanged (docs only).\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Diagnostic + roadmap.** No code change. Fix to be implemented next session.\n\nRefs #286\n",
